DeviceDex Privacy Policy
Effective date: September 12, 2026
This Privacy Policy explains how DeviceDex, including the Discord bot HarmonyDex, handles information when you use the Service.
1. Information We May Collect
When you interact with HarmonyDex, DeviceDex may process or store information necessary for the bot to function, including:
- Discord user IDs.
- Discord server/guild IDs.
- Discord channel IDs when required for bot configuration or commands.
- DeviceDex/HarmonyDex collection and game progress.
- Virtual inventory, trades, statistics, settings, and related game data.
- Command usage and interaction information.
- Moderation or administrative records related to the Service.
- Technical logs, error information, and diagnostic data.
Discord usernames, display names, avatars, and similar public Discord information may also be accessed when necessary to display features of the bot.
2. Message Content
DeviceDex does not intentionally collect unrelated private conversations.
The bot may receive information that you deliberately send through commands, buttons, forms, or other Discord interactions when that information is required to perform the requested feature.
Discord itself may provide additional information to bots according to the permissions granted to them.
3. How Information Is Used
Information processed by DeviceDex may be used to:
- Operate HarmonyDex.
- Store your collection and game progress.
- Process commands, trades, and other interactions.
- Configure the bot for Discord servers.
- Prevent abuse, cheating, spam, or exploitation.
- Investigate technical problems.
- Maintain security and reliability.
- Improve existing features and develop new ones.
We do not sell personal information to advertisers.
4. Legal Basis
Where applicable under laws such as the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), information may be processed because it is necessary to provide the Service you requested, because there is a legitimate interest in operating and securing the Service, or because you have provided consent where consent is required.
5. Data Sharing
Information may be shared only when reasonably necessary, including with:
- Infrastructure or hosting providers used to operate DeviceDex.
- Discord, as the platform through which the Service operates.
- Service operators or administrators who need access for technical, moderation, or security purposes.
- Authorities where disclosure is legally required.
DeviceDex does not sell or rent user information.
6. Data Retention
Information is kept only for as long as reasonably necessary to operate DeviceDex, maintain game progress, enforce rules, resolve disputes, maintain security, or comply with legal obligations.
Some information may be removed automatically after it is no longer needed.
Backups may temporarily retain deleted information until those backups are rotated or removed.
7. Data Deletion
You may request deletion of personal information associated with your Discord account.
A deletion request may result in loss of your HarmonyDex collection, statistics, inventory, settings, and other stored progress.
To request deletion, contact:
Email: YOUR_EMAIL
Support server: YOUR_SUPPORT_SERVER
Include your Discord user ID so the relevant records can be located.
We may need to verify that the request actually comes from the account owner because, surprisingly, deleting someone else's account because a random Discord user asked would be a somewhat terrible privacy system.
8. Your Privacy Rights
Depending on where you live, you may have rights relating to your personal information, including the right to:
- Request access to information associated with you.
- Request correction of inaccurate information.
- Request deletion of information.
- Object to or restrict certain processing.
- Request a copy of certain information in a portable format.
- Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.
- Submit a complaint to the relevant data-protection authority.
These rights may be subject to legal limitations.
9. Children's Privacy
DeviceDex is intended for users who are legally permitted to use Discord.
We do not knowingly collect personal information from users who are below the minimum age required to use Discord.
10. Security
Reasonable technical and organizational measures are used to protect stored information.
However, no online system can guarantee absolute security.
Users should never send passwords, authentication tokens, payment credentials, or other sensitive credentials to HarmonyDex.
11. Third-Party Services
DeviceDex depends on Discord and potentially other infrastructure providers.
Use of those services may also be governed by their respective privacy policies.
DeviceDex is not responsible for the privacy practices of unrelated third-party services.
12. Changes to This Policy
This Privacy Policy may be updated as DeviceDex develops or as legal requirements change.
The effective date at the top of this page will be updated when significant changes are made.
